# Claim the Firstborn can target a creature its caster already controls (its ruling): Bot1's own Hired Blade attacked and is
# tapped; Claim in the second main phase untaps it (the Untap sentence) and gives it haste (CR 702.10) until end of turn
# (CR 611.2a), after which control did not change hands. Bot1 plays Mountain on turn 1, the Blade via Black Lotus.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Black Lotus
Hired Blade
Claim the Firstborn
Mountain x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: B)
Bot1.Hand.Hired Blade.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Attack(Hired Blade > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Hired Blade.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Claim the Firstborn.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Hired Blade)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
? Bot1.Mana = 
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Hired Blade.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Hired Blade.Keywords = Flash; Haste
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Hired Blade.Keywords = Flash

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Hired Blade; Mountain; Mountain
Bot1.Graveyard = Claim the Firstborn; Black Lotus
Bot2.Life = 17
